B.a62=new A.ec("1. Introduction",'Experimentar AB (Org. nr: 559578-3274), operating under the brand "GettaShower" ("we", "our", or "us"), operates the Getta Shower mobile application and related services. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our app, including in the European Economic Area (EEA) and the United Kingdom. Please read it carefully. By using our services, you agree to the practices described here.')
B.a61=new A.ec("2. Data controller and contact","The data controller responsible for your personal data is Experimentar AB (Org. nr: 559578-3274), Molnv\xe4dersgatan 8 Lgh 1301, 418 35 G\xf6teborg, Sweden. You may contact us for privacy-related requests or questions at info@gettashower.com. If you are in the EEA, you may also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority.")
B.a5K=new A.ec("3. What data we collect","We collect information you provide (e.g. account registration, profile details, listing submissions, free-shower submissions, reviews, moderation reports, and support messages), information generated by your use of the service (e.g. saved places, trust signals, and host/company onboarding records), and technical/device information (e.g. device type, identifiers, and log data) where necessary for the service, security, or legal compliance. We do not collect more than is necessary for the purposes described in this policy.")
B.a68=new A.ec("4. Legal basis (EEA/UK)","Where applicable law requires a legal basis: we process your data for the performance of our contract with you (e.g. providing account access, listing discovery, and review features), for our legitimate interests (e.g. security, fraud prevention, analytics, moderation, and improving the service) where not overridden by your rights, and, where we ask for your consent, based on that consent. You may withdraw consent at any time where processing is based on consent, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before withdrawal.")
B.a5I=new A.ec("5. How we use your data","We use your data to provide, maintain, and improve our services; to power map/listing discovery; to show and moderate listings, reviews, and reports; to apply trust and safety controls (including automated moderation thresholds); to communicate with you about your account and the service; to ensure security and prevent fraud; to comply with legal obligations; and, where permitted, for analytics and product improvement. We do not sell your personal data to third parties for their marketing.")
B.a65=new A.ec("6. Platform operations and authorised staff access",'A limited number of authorised Getta Shower personnel ("operators") may access personal data held in our systems when this is necessary to operate, secure, and improve the platform. This may include, for example: account and profile details; messages, reviews, or moderation reports you send us; facility and company records for hosts; and compliance or fraud-prevention metadata required to keep the marketplace safe. Such access is purpose-limited (for example: customer support, listing moderation, abuse prevention, legal compliance, and engineering incident response). Access is granted only to trained staff who need it for their role, subject to internal policies, technical controls, and logging where appropriate. Depending on the processing activity, we rely on the legal bases described in section 4 (typically performance of a contract, legitimate interests balanced against your rights, and/or legal obligation). This section does not change your rights in section 8.')
B.a5J=new A.ec("7. Data retention","We retain your data only as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes in this policy, including legal, tax, or regulatory requirements. Certain moderation and trust datasets may have fixed retention windows and may be deleted automatically after the applicable retention period, unless legal hold or another legal obligation applies. When data is no longer needed, we delete or anonymise it. You may request erasure of your data subject to applicable exceptions.")
B.a64=new A.ec("8. Your rights",'Depending on your location, you may have the right to: access your personal data; rectify inaccurate data; request erasure ("right to be forgotten"); restrict processing; data portability; object to certain processing; withdraw consent where processing is based on consent; and lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. To exercise these rights, contact us using the details provided in the app or on our website. We will respond within the timeframes required by applicable law (e.g. one month under GDPR).')
B.a69=new A.ec("9. International transfers","Your data may be processed in countries outside your country of residence, including countries that may not provide the same level of data protection. Where we transfer data from the EEA or UK to third countries, we implement appropriate safeguards (e.g. standard contractual clauses or other mechanisms approved by the relevant authorities) as required by applicable law.")
B.a5X=new A.ec("10. Security","We implement technical and organisational measures to protect your data against unauthorised access, loss, or misuse. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure; we encourage you to use a strong password and keep your account details confidential.")
